The file beside this one — `highlight.tex` — is skylighting's, taken
verbatim from the preamble pandoc 3.8.2.1 writes for a standalone LaTeX
document containing a highlighted code block:

    pandoc -s -t latex doc.md

It is `styleToLaTeX pygments` from **`skylighting-format-latex`**, which
is BSD-3, "(C) 2016-2022 John MacFarlane" — the same footing as the HTML
stylesheet in `crates/ferrodoc-html/styles/`, and for the same reason:
skylighting's GPL is on the wrapper that bundles KDE's syntax XML, which
this project does not read. `crates/ferrodoc-html/styles/LICENSE` has the
full notice and the three-package split; `THIRD-PARTY.md` carries it to
the binaries, where BSD-3 asks for it.

